gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_1=This button *adds a recipe to a plan*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_2=This is a *recipe in a plan*. It does nothing yet: nothing has told it how much to make.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_3={M} *Middle mouse* to pan.\n{W} *Scroll* to zoom.\n{L} *Left click* to pan, or drag things around.\nTry it, then press next.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_4={K} *W A S D* or the *arrow keys* to pan.\n{K} *Page Up* and *Page Down*, or *+* and *-*, to zoom.\nTry it, then press next.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_5=You can *pin a number* and it calculates the other numbers.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_6=Or pin the *machine count*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_7=Or pin an *input*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_8=Set the machine's *tier* here.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_9=Power use is shown here, but machines *don't need to be wired to power*. The circuit is also shown.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_10=This is the *settings panel*. If it has any settings, you can *pin* them to show them on the card.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_11=You can *clone* machines.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_12=Drag an *input* or an *output* to make it a *drawer*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_13=Or bring one in from *NEI*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_14=*Drag from a drawer* to wire it. Set the drawer's *rate* and it applies to every machine wired to it.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_15=*Arrange* untangles the plan, and *Fit* brings all of it into view.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_16=The *overview* lists everything in the plan. You can set your inputs and outputs from here too.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_17={b:Blue} is always something coming into your plan, and {o:Orange} is always something leaving it. Nothing else is shown in those colours.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_18=Your *machines* are here too: set how many from here, as on their cards.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_19=Hold *Shift* to select more than one. Then you can *merge* machines, to run two recipes on one machine.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_20=*Undo* and *redo* are up here.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_21=These buttons change *the way numbers are shown*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_22=Add as many recipes to a plan as you like.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_23=Click an input to find *what makes it*. A recipe added from there comes in *already wired*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_24=The acid is set and one electrolyzer is pinned *exactly*, but it can't keep up. The plan has to bring in the rest of the oxygen anyway: a *forced input*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_25=*Right-click* an output to find *what uses it*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_26=Electrolyzer pinned *exactly* high, mixer pinned *exactly* low: more oxygen is made than used. The excess leaves the plan as a *forced output*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_27=The excess can leave at more than one machine. The *slider* sets the split: oxygen out of the electrolyzer, or extra acid out of the reactor. *Auto* hands it back to the solver.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_28=This key's menu also makes a product drawer *trash*: it voids what comes in, and leaves your outputs.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_29=And back to a *product*. On *Any* it takes whatever comes out; set a rate and the plan works toward it.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_30=This section is for *non-recipe machines*, mostly power generation.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_31=You can also *plan power*. This distillation tower makes enough benzene to run this many HV gas turbines.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_32=Here's how you make a *new plan*.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_33=Sign in and your plans save as you edit, on any computer. *Share* invites someone to build the plan with you, live.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_34=*Plans* has all your plans, and the ones people shared with you.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_35=*Community* is where people post their plans. You can browse them here.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_36=Annotations are possible with *sticky notes*. Right-click anywhere to make one.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_37=*Place in the world* puts a machine over the spot you'll build it. *Pin to the screen* keeps it in a corner while you play.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_38=While you play, the *minimap* shows your plan and the *pin list* your pinned machines. Set both up under the gear.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_39=*Add to a task* puts machines on a task board, with how many to build.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_40=A *task* holds notes, a checklist, comments and who is on it. Drag it across the columns as the work goes.
gtnhplanner.ui.tutorial.step_41=That's everything! Found a bug, or have an idea? *Feedback* sends it from the game. Questions about your own setup do well in GTNH Planner's thread on the *GT New Horizons Discord*.
